From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Botond Lovasz <botilovasz@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:48:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Let GPU clients that release on unbind not block a vfio
 switch

dcgm-exporter keeps every GPU open, and with its bind/unbind watch
(detached-GPU support, driver 590+ / DCGM 4.5+) it lets go of a GPU once
the nvidia driver starts unbinding it. The holder scan rightly counts it,
so a switch to vfio could never start while dcgm-exporter runs, short of
evicting it first.

--vfio-unbind-releasing-holders (VFIO_UNBIND_RELEASING_HOLDERS) names
such clients by executable. They no longer block the switch; any other
holder, or one whose executable cannot be read, still does. Empty by
default, so nothing changes unless it is set.
